WEBVTT

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:17.130
Nusumareta kako wo

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:20.330
Sagashitsuzukete

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.420
Ore wa samayou

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:27.130
Mishiranu machi wo

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:32.040
Honou no nioi shimitsuite

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:33.750
Museru

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:37.630
Sayonara wa itta hazu da

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.540
Wakareta hazu sa

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.790
Jigoku wo mireba

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.330
Kokoro ga kawaku

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:52.750
Tatakai wa akita no sa

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.540
Sadame to areba

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:00.790
Kokoro wo kimeru

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:05.960
Sottoshite oite kure

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.750
Ashita ni

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:15.250
Aa tsunagaru kyou gurai

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:52.830
Gilgamesh 6th and 7th combined
space forces now approaching.

00:01:53.790 --> 00:01:56.790
The question is how the Balarant forces
on Quent will oppose them.

00:01:56.790 --> 00:01:58.790
I don't see any way they could win.

00:02:00.130 --> 00:02:04.000
Quent's 3,000-year-old veil
of mystery is being lifted.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:08.000
And it looks like both the Gilgamesh and the
Balarant are setting out to find the answers here.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:10.460
We can't go on lurking in the shadows!

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:15.040
But, sir! Even the Balarant can't go
up against a fleet that big!

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:19.000
We're in the same boat they are.

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:21.000
But we have to do something!

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:24.210
Sir! We've regained contact with
our detachment on Quent!

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:26.830
Killy here!

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:28.710
Sir, it's Arron.

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:31.670
All of our AT troops have vanished.

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:33.130
What? Again?

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:36.920
I hate to sound so unscientific,
but they were annihilated.

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:39.540
Vanished, and never reappeared.

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:44.880
I believe Quent's ancient technology
has fully awakened.

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:47.420
Awake... I thought so...

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:51.290
Hm? You sound like you had
a premonition about this, sir.

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:55.040
We may not have much info on Quent,

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:57.380
but records show this has happened before.

00:02:57.380 --> 00:03:00.670
You must know there's a large
Gilgamesh fleet approaching.

00:03:00.670 --> 00:03:05.000
But Gomor is completely under
Balarant control, sir.

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:10.920
Our operation may be stalled,
but there's still a chance.

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:13.420
We'll wait for both sides
to start fighting each other.

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:15.540
I agree, sir.

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:19.540
We can use the confusion of battle
to steal Proto One back.

00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:25.290
The Balarant ships standing by in the air must be
in contact with the commander down here.

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:27.710
We'll contact you again when we have more data.

00:03:27.710 --> 00:03:29.290
Until then, sir.

00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:34.830
Premonition

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:46.710
We've got the upper hand,
no matter how you look at it.

00:03:47.250 --> 00:03:49.040
But they'll be desperate.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:51.000
They won't hand it over so easily.

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:52.710
Battle is unavoidable.

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:57.250
Sir, we have a message from High Command.

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:58.630
Right. Patch it through.

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:02.540
General Battentain!

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:05.670
We've joined with Hallory's fleet
and are approaching Gomor.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:08.540
I see. Are you ready for battle?

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:11.920
Yes, sir. We're at DefCon 2
and can attack at any time.

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:16.380
Excellent. The combined fleet
you command has a vital duty.

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:19.670
It's a gamble, but you must complete this mission!

00:04:19.670 --> 00:04:22.380
Yes, well...

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:25.080
I understand your concern.

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:28.460
We have to move fast, so I'll keep this simple.

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:31.790
Quent is a mystery world which,
until 3,000 years ago,

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:34.460
was proud of its advanced technology.

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:36.130
I've heard all that.

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:38.210
The question is what's happening here now?

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:39.670
It seems that technology has reawakened.

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:41.380
What? You mean...?

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:44.170
Our personal forces on Quent have vanished.

00:04:44.170 --> 00:04:46.170
I know it's hard to believe, but it's true.

00:04:46.830 --> 00:04:50.210
There's a lot we don't know about
Quent's ancient technology.

00:04:50.210 --> 00:04:52.630
Why has it suddenly been reawakened now?

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:54.710
You're saying it's not just a coincidence?

00:04:54.710 --> 00:04:59.920
Don't you see that someone has
opened the door to Quent's mysteries?

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:01.210
The Prototype, maybe?

00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:04.880
I won't say anything at this stage,

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:07.080
but there may be some connection.

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:11.290
If we search Quent, we may find
some unexpected things.

00:05:12.170 --> 00:05:14.330
I'd have to agree, sir.

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:18.830
Lepard! Even if that whole fleet is annihilated,
it may still help us solve this mystery!

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:21.500
Yes... You may be right, sir.

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:25.290
I'm sure I don't need to spell out
what I expect of you.

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:27.000
Understood, sir!

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:29.790
I'll open discussion with the Balarant at once!

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:55.830
Hey, soldier. The ship looks like it's stopped.

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:57.330
Where are we?

00:05:57.330 --> 00:05:58.750
Planet Quent.

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:02.710
Food! Food! Food! Food!

00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:05.130
Wasn't Ru Shako from Quent?

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:08.040
Better eat your food before you end up
eating a stray shot, instead.

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:09.580
We may be going into battle.

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:12.580
Jeez, why'd you hafta bring us
to a dangerous place?

00:06:12.580 --> 00:06:14.290
We didn't do anything wrong!

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:19.380
What, Dabo Fish rations again?
For crying out loud!

00:06:19.420 --> 00:06:23.540
Look, the stuff you're getting is
a lot better than what we get!

00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:27.170
That's 'cuz you're such important guests.

00:06:27.170 --> 00:06:28.750
What's that mean?

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:31.080
What are you guys up to?

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:35.130
We're gonna use you to steal back the PS.

00:06:35.130 --> 00:06:36.250
You're what?

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:38.710
Eat up, while you're still alive to enjoy it.

00:06:39.670 --> 00:06:43.630
You guys'll never win a war eating this crap!

00:06:43.630 --> 00:06:45.710
"Steal back the PS..."

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:47.790
Are Chirico and Fyana here?

00:06:47.790 --> 00:06:49.790
Who can say?

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:53.710
If he meant that Chirico's here...

00:06:53.710 --> 00:06:54.830
Then...

00:06:54.830 --> 00:06:56.670
Then we're in luck!

00:07:11.580 --> 00:07:16.460
This is Rear Admiral Fermeaud Lepard,
commander of the Gilgamesh 7th Space Fleet.

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:19.330
I wish to speak with the
Balarant commanding officer.

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:24.540
In the name of Gen. Detel Battentain
of the Gilgamesh High Command,

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:26.790
I demand that we open
formal discussions with you.

00:07:26.790 --> 00:07:28.540
Reply at once!

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:32.330
I repeat, in the name of General Detel Battentain,

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:34.880
I demand we open formal discussions with you.

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:36.710
Reply at once!

00:07:37.500 --> 00:07:39.250
Sir, we have to attack!

00:07:39.250 --> 00:07:41.880
You think we can go head-to-head
and beat them?

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:45.830
If we go along with this,
they'll attack us for sure!

00:07:45.830 --> 00:07:48.080
We'll have to face them either way!

00:07:48.080 --> 00:07:49.830
Sir, what do we do?

00:07:53.630 --> 00:07:54.460
Sir!

00:07:54.750 --> 00:07:57.420
This is Balarant Colonel Rochina.

00:07:57.630 --> 00:07:59.460
I agree to open discussions.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:04.000
I will meet with you at the Gomor spaceport
in three hours. That is all.

00:08:05.170 --> 00:08:07.380
This complicates things.

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:08.580
Yeah...

00:08:57.960 --> 00:08:59.630
What's going to happen?

00:08:59.630 --> 00:09:02.290
I just hope they'll fight.

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:29.830
I'm pleased you agreed to these talks, sir.

00:09:29.830 --> 00:09:31.830
I'm pleased to hear that, Admiral Lepard.

00:09:32.580 --> 00:09:38.420
We used to have an
Intelligence Officer named Rochina.

00:09:38.420 --> 00:09:44.000
But a Gilgamesh officer would
never defect to the Balarant.

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:45.380
Pardon my mistake.

00:09:45.380 --> 00:09:47.380
I don't know about that.

00:09:47.380 --> 00:09:49.630
War can be a complicated thing.

00:09:49.630 --> 00:09:52.750
One must be ready to react to
a myriad of changing situations.

00:09:54.750 --> 00:09:57.750
I've a message from General Battentain.

00:10:00.080 --> 00:10:02.540
You are to hand over the Prototype
without any trouble.

00:10:02.540 --> 00:10:03.380
"The Prototype?"

00:10:03.380 --> 00:10:04.460
Yes.

00:10:04.460 --> 00:10:07.710
The Prototype you've been
kindly taking care of for us.

00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:09.290
There must be some mistake.

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:13.000
It's true, I ran into her on that hellhole, Sunsa.

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:16.000
But she ran off with a soldier named Chirico.

00:10:17.630 --> 00:10:21.670
I'm sorry, Admiral. That case is closed.

00:10:21.670 --> 00:10:23.790
And I've no other information to give you.

00:10:23.790 --> 00:10:25.210
Col. Rochina!

00:10:25.210 --> 00:10:29.290
Gen. Battentain demands you
turn her over unconditionally!

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:32.630
And I repeat, she isn't on Quent.

00:10:38.960 --> 00:10:40.330
Hey there, Col. Rochina!

00:10:40.330 --> 00:10:43.460
You finally let us go and we got captured again.

00:10:43.460 --> 00:10:44.830
Helluva screw-up, huh?

00:10:44.830 --> 00:10:48.500
No kidding. We should've
stayed with you and Chirico.

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:54.420
Shall we begin these talks fresh?

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:56.710
If you're prepared to, that is.

00:10:56.960 --> 00:11:00.380
We're witnesses. To Chirico and Fyana...

00:11:00.380 --> 00:11:02.460
"Valuable guests." Shit!

00:11:02.460 --> 00:11:03.750
C'mon, move!

00:11:03.750 --> 00:11:04.670
Piss off.

00:11:10.580 --> 00:11:12.170
Admiral Lepard!

00:11:12.170 --> 00:11:15.960
We will return the Prototype to you
at 18:00 hours, Quent time.

00:11:16.790 --> 00:11:19.920
I'm glad you decided to be reasonable about this.

00:11:19.920 --> 00:11:23.290
I'm glad we could resolve this peacefully.

00:11:23.290 --> 00:11:26.670
Gen. Battentain will be
extremely grateful as well.

00:11:29.330 --> 00:11:32.790
I suggest you keep cool
till this is over, Col. Rochina.

00:11:33.210 --> 00:11:34.540
If you'll excuse me...

00:11:42.500 --> 00:11:44.330
Looks like the talks are over.

00:11:44.330 --> 00:11:45.710
How disappointing.

00:11:45.710 --> 00:11:47.960
I was hoping they'd break down.

00:11:47.960 --> 00:11:51.880
But Rochina isn't one to give up so easily.

00:11:51.880 --> 00:11:53.420
I certainly hope so!

00:11:57.380 --> 00:12:00.040
Sir, are you giving them the Prototype?

00:12:00.040 --> 00:12:00.920
Yes.

00:12:00.920 --> 00:12:04.210
But that means giving up our whole mission!

00:12:04.460 --> 00:12:06.880
We can steal her back any time.

00:12:06.880 --> 00:12:10.170
Our problem right now is
getting the Gilgamesh to leave.

00:12:10.170 --> 00:12:11.420
Uh, but...

00:12:11.420 --> 00:12:14.420
Just watch. I've an idea.

00:12:30.670 --> 00:12:33.000
You're what the Gilgamesh are here for.

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:33.920
I know.

00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:35.130
I won't let them have you.

00:12:36.290 --> 00:12:37.880
I'm afraid.

00:12:38.130 --> 00:12:39.710
That's why I'll...

00:12:39.710 --> 00:12:42.750
No! Not for me, Chirico.

00:12:43.130 --> 00:12:45.290
Don't investigate Quent any further!

00:12:46.080 --> 00:12:47.670
You're human.

00:12:47.670 --> 00:12:50.130
A normal man. I believe that!

00:12:50.540 --> 00:12:53.040
So, please, let's just get away
from here, Chirico.

00:12:56.630 --> 00:12:59.080
And I'd just given you my word.

00:12:59.080 --> 00:13:00.500
Damn it all!

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:03.040
They had those three
good-for-nothings with them!

00:13:03.040 --> 00:13:04.170
Gotho and the others?

00:13:04.170 --> 00:13:06.500
Yes, them. Killing them
would have been a mercy.

00:13:08.380 --> 00:13:11.960
Anyway, the Balarant
can't refuse these demands.

00:13:14.790 --> 00:13:16.420
You're planning to give them Fyana?

00:13:16.920 --> 00:13:20.330
Yes! If I don't, they'll attack!

00:13:20.750 --> 00:13:24.170
I can't give Quent to the Gilgamesh! Not now!

00:13:36.540 --> 00:13:39.790
We were tailor-made witnesses for them, huh?

00:13:39.790 --> 00:13:41.750
Quit talking about it, Coconna.

00:13:41.750 --> 00:13:44.500
We won't solve anything
by getting all worked up.

00:13:44.500 --> 00:13:47.170
But don't you feel sorry for Fyana?

00:13:47.170 --> 00:13:48.460
Yeah, I guess.

00:13:48.460 --> 00:13:51.330
Fyana... I bet he'll do it.

00:13:51.750 --> 00:13:52.710
What?

00:13:52.710 --> 00:13:54.210
Chirico'll do something.

00:13:55.500 --> 00:13:58.290
He'll never stand by and let them take her.

00:13:58.500 --> 00:14:01.290
Right! And he might save us, too!

00:14:01.670 --> 00:14:04.330
Assuming he comes before they
decide to just execute us.

00:14:04.330 --> 00:14:05.630
Right...

00:14:09.460 --> 00:14:14.040
You may feel the first stage is a success,
but the real question is when they return her.

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:16.500
I doubt he'll give her back without a fight!

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:19.420
I agree. He'll probably try a sneak attack.

00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:21.250
Glad you see that!

00:14:21.250 --> 00:14:24.500
Go to DefCon 1 and don't screw this up!

00:14:24.500 --> 00:14:26.250
Leave this to me, sir.

00:14:26.750 --> 00:14:29.750
Admiral Lepard, when I report to
the High Command,

00:14:29.750 --> 00:14:31.750
I'll be sure to mention
your next command posting.

00:14:32.210 --> 00:14:34.250
Thank you, General!

00:14:56.250 --> 00:14:58.750
Are you the escorts for the commander's ship?

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:02.170
Yeah, we both got the order.

00:15:02.170 --> 00:15:03.920
Hey! I'll meet you on board.

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:04.750
Right!

00:15:11.380 --> 00:15:12.380
Going to try for it?

00:15:12.380 --> 00:15:13.710
Will you help me?

00:15:13.710 --> 00:15:14.790
I can't.

00:15:15.500 --> 00:15:17.540
My people don't fight on this world.

00:15:18.250 --> 00:15:20.040
I'm a Quentian.

00:15:20.790 --> 00:15:21.880
I understand.

00:15:26.580 --> 00:15:27.710
Hey!

00:15:28.580 --> 00:15:29.790
What?

00:15:29.790 --> 00:15:31.250
Let him go instead.

00:15:31.250 --> 00:15:33.000
That's against orders!

00:15:38.830 --> 00:15:39.710
Thanks.

00:15:39.710 --> 00:15:40.670
Chirico...

00:15:41.830 --> 00:15:42.830
It's all right.

00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:44.630
I'm sorry.

00:15:48.290 --> 00:15:49.960
It can't be helped, right?

00:16:04.630 --> 00:16:07.130
He's only taking that few?

00:16:07.130 --> 00:16:09.080
Looks like he won't try anything after all.

00:16:09.290 --> 00:16:11.380
He's really going to give them Proto One.

00:16:14.630 --> 00:16:17.000
What are they really playing at?

00:16:25.710 --> 00:16:27.210
Use docking gate A.

00:16:27.210 --> 00:16:27.960
Roger!

00:16:27.960 --> 00:16:29.500
Prep for main engine start.

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:30.460
Roger!

00:16:31.380 --> 00:16:33.710
They'll treat you well.

00:16:34.500 --> 00:16:35.710
Don't worry.

00:16:43.290 --> 00:16:45.460
We'll be clearing the stratosphere shortly, sir.

00:16:46.380 --> 00:16:47.670
This is Rochina.

00:16:47.670 --> 00:16:50.580
Admiral, as promised,
I'm handing over the Prototype.

00:16:51.630 --> 00:16:54.500
This is Lepard.
I'm pleased to see you're cooperating.

00:16:54.500 --> 00:16:56.880
We'd like to know your vessel's complement.

00:16:56.880 --> 00:17:00.960
Myself and the Prototype,
two escort ATs and two pilots.

00:17:00.960 --> 00:17:02.040
Six in all.

00:17:02.710 --> 00:17:05.880
Roger that. Please dock via the rear hatch.

00:17:05.880 --> 00:17:08.710
And please keep any other ships
from approaching.

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:10.000
Roger.

00:17:33.040 --> 00:17:35.000
A peaceful resolution.

00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:36.960
Thanks to your gentle favors.

00:17:37.380 --> 00:17:39.130
Well then, we'll be taking her.

00:17:39.920 --> 00:17:41.330
One moment!

00:17:42.380 --> 00:17:43.920
Is there something else?

00:17:43.920 --> 00:17:48.750
Now that you have her, please withdraw
the Gilgamesh fleet from Quent.

00:17:52.290 --> 00:17:54.750
Didn't I say this was unconditional, Col. Rochina?

00:17:54.750 --> 00:17:57.880
My fleet will remain here for the time being.

00:17:58.380 --> 00:17:59.380
What?

00:17:59.380 --> 00:18:02.920
Of course, we'll be landing
occupation troops in Gomor as well.

00:18:02.920 --> 00:18:06.000
For the peaceful administration
by both armies, naturally.

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:07.330
Unacceptable!

00:18:07.330 --> 00:18:09.710
Now that you have the Prototype,
I demand that you leave!

00:18:09.710 --> 00:18:13.790
I'm sorry. Gen. Battentain was
quite adamant in his orders.

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:25.960
Fyana, run!

00:18:25.960 --> 00:18:27.080
Chirico!

00:18:27.080 --> 00:18:28.830
The agreement's blown! Attack!

00:18:32.790 --> 00:18:33.830
Chirico!

00:19:06.170 --> 00:19:07.500
Open fire!

00:19:10.080 --> 00:19:11.420
Commence attack!

00:20:46.330 --> 00:20:47.330
Something's coming?

00:20:47.330 --> 00:20:49.420
It's Chirico! And he's close!

00:20:53.920 --> 00:20:55.670
Chirico! In here! We're in here!

00:20:56.170 --> 00:20:58.540
Lemme go! I told you where they are!

00:20:58.540 --> 00:21:00.040
Lemme go, you bastard!

00:21:00.670 --> 00:21:01.670
All right, in here!

00:21:13.630 --> 00:21:15.040
Chirico, my man!

00:21:15.040 --> 00:21:16.960
You showed up after all!

00:21:17.580 --> 00:21:19.500
Get out of here! There's a hangar to the left!

00:21:19.500 --> 00:21:20.960
Use a shuttle to escape!

00:21:20.960 --> 00:21:22.170
What about you?

00:21:22.170 --> 00:21:23.420
C'mon, lemme go!

00:21:24.290 --> 00:21:27.670
I was nice to you guys, right?
Get him to let me go!

00:21:53.330 --> 00:21:55.040
Vanilla! This one looks ready to go!

00:21:55.040 --> 00:21:55.880
Right!

00:21:56.540 --> 00:21:57.540
Okay...

00:22:00.250 --> 00:22:01.830
Vanilla, are we gonna be all right?

00:22:01.830 --> 00:22:03.500
It's gonna be close.

00:22:03.880 --> 00:22:04.880
Leave it to me.

00:22:09.250 --> 00:22:11.670
Okay, Chirico! It's your call!

00:22:12.290 --> 00:22:13.750
Anytime you're ready.

00:22:36.290 --> 00:22:38.500
The battle had turned
more intense than I'd expected.

00:22:39.040 --> 00:22:42.170
And then, somewhere in my body, I felt it.

00:22:43.170 --> 00:22:44.170
A premonition.

00:22:44.710 --> 00:22:48.750
Yes, one from the darkness,
for only me to know.

00:22:50.210 --> 00:22:52.880
And that's when the whole
horrible thing happened.

00:22:54.960 --> 00:22:56.380
Next Episode

00:22:57.130 --> 00:23:01.170
It grows. An expansive energy is released.

00:23:01.630 --> 00:23:03.630
Huge ships caught in it become fireballs.

00:23:03.830 --> 00:23:06.000
A fleet vanishes without a trace.

00:23:06.790 --> 00:23:11.500
From across 3,000 years,
an ancient energy blasts forth.

00:23:11.500 --> 00:23:13.630
War. Ambition.

00:23:13.790 --> 00:23:18.170
Chirico, what will be triggered off when
the mysterious intelligence is contacted?

00:23:18.500 --> 00:23:20.170
Next time, "Disaster"

00:23:20.630 --> 00:23:22.460
The skies of Quent will burn.

00:23:21.000 --> 00:23:24.960
Disaster

00:23:21.000 --> 00:23:24.960
Next Time

00:23:43.210 --> 00:23:46.670
Samishii toki mo

00:23:46.670 --> 00:23:50.210
Kanashii toki mo

00:23:50.210 --> 00:23:56.580
Itsumo anata ga me ni ukabu

00:23:57.080 --> 00:24:00.630
Hitori no toki mo

00:24:00.630 --> 00:24:04.040
Aitai toki mo

00:24:04.040 --> 00:24:10.290
Itsumo anata wa mune no naka

00:24:10.290 --> 00:24:13.790
Tooku hanarete itemo

00:24:13.790 --> 00:24:17.210
Tatoe wakarete itemo

00:24:17.380 --> 00:24:23.710
Kono yo no hikari to tomo ni mabushiku

00:24:24.080 --> 00:24:30.040
Ano hi no anata ga...
